      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_1d3a483b6d33160223271fe41a6c8599ce783d5b9ab01da15aba94159ebf0692"
      ],
      "text": "Each conversation turn is embedded as a semantic vector and queried against a memory graph via cosine similarity; hits are injected into the conversation, optionally after verification by a memory sideagent."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_8c7d255f2686db133ffc6430b5e57137d9ff644101c1a5efb4e457729e319c5c",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "memory-state",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b",
          "git_sha": "99abe8fa61fb3004f509ebbc9cadb884efa16b70",
          "line_end": 289,
          "line_start": 287,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "1jehuang/jcode",
          "url": "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b/README.md#L287-L289"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_1d3a483b6d33160223271fe41a6c8599ce783d5b9ab01da15aba94159ebf0692"
      ],
      "text": "Memories are extracted by a memory sideagent at triggers such as semantic drift, a K-turn interval, or session end, and added to the memory graph."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_882610b9676cf4753adab4f2c626c4225531e12cc5205089b5e0efb0d26b6048",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "memory-state",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b",
          "git_sha": "99abe8fa61fb3004f509ebbc9cadb884efa16b70",
          "line_end": 291,
          "line_start": 291,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "1jehuang/jcode",
          "url": "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b/README.md#L291-L291"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_18eacb2001e4c88a03d72d68d7c6cad6b45859b1c00d27ca8bb20300454d4d9d"
      ],
      "text": "Besides passive background recall, jcode provides explicit memory tools for active search/store, plus session search performing traditional RAG over previous sessions."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_f675a67985250349fafd70ccc92c0370485350ded68446fc7c749e17a1dcc20b",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "memory-state",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b",
          "git_sha": "99abe8fa61fb3004f509ebbc9cadb884efa16b70",
          "line_end": 293,
          "line_start": 293,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "1jehuang/jcode",
          "url": "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b/README.md#L293-L293"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_3e589ce2ea817ee4babe3e896d25267acff2330efc3414ba8935a1493bb4aa23"
      ],
      "text": "An ambient mode periodically consolidates memories, reorganizing them and checking for staleness and conflicts."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_3e0adbd6ce51b05c6f2d4d1f6234706c1011a17c36a8530edefbd67001bdb400",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b",
          "git_sha": "99abe8fa61fb3004f509ebbc9cadb884efa16b70",
          "line_end": 330,
          "line_start": 330,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "1jehuang/jcode",
          "url": "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b/README.md#L330-L330"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_45621a313931a309eb6a58e5f49e2a28a133155a15d49563ec69f35984863121"
      ],
      "text": "Multiple agents spawned in the same repo are managed by a server: when one agent edits a file another has read, the server notifies the reader, which can ignore it or check the diff; agents can DM, broadcast, or message repo-scoped peers."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_a133509c1534db3799addcdf629d5139f7dd41f5ada37c9dd1cb8038e7e4c7f6",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "orchestration",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b",
          "git_sha": "99abe8fa61fb3004f509ebbc9cadb884efa16b70",
          "line_end": 342,
          "line_start": 342,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "1jehuang/jcode",
          "url": "https://github.com/1jehuang/jcode/blob/37159430c3d02545fd7c10b0bd13e754b49f871b/README.md#L342-L342"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_8225cbf7e16059afb34f5d0effc747f1563bde4a76bf73345436776040aa666f"
      ],
      "text": "Agents have a swarm tool to autonomously spawn teammates for parallel work, turning the main agent into a coordinator; groups, messaging channels, and completion statuses are managed automatically, headed or headless."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_8a5ded1a1c5b93ca80c76384e555bc464ac45aeebf72322a9a6605fb24a0f77e",
